Zedbee is a defensive code-quality and security analysis tool for JavaScript
and TypeScript repositories. Its intended use is to review code that the user
owns or is authorized to assess, including staged changes and committed branch
changes before they are accepted into a project.

Security-relevant capabilities include detecting possible embedded secrets,
matching structural security patterns, and checking dependency versions against
known vulnerability records. Such findings can reveal weaknesses in a codebase;
users must not use them to gain unauthorized access or harm other parties.

Zedbee does not validate discovered credentials against live services or exploit
the issues it reports. Analysis uses managed configuration and isolated source
snapshots. Optional online checks and their metadata disclosures, local report
retention, and source-excerpt behavior are described in docs/privacy.md.

Report suspected security vulnerabilities privately to security@zedbee.dev.
See SECURITY.md for reporting guidance and docs/structural-security-coverage.md
for the limits of the structural checks. Static analysis is not a guarantee
that a repository is free of vulnerabilities.
